GEM native workbench — upstream notices

Ubuntu Update Manager
- The GTK interaction model was informed by Ubuntu's UpdateManager source, including Gtk.TreeStore, Gtk.ToggleButton and toggled, Gio actions, GLib timeouts, cancellable backend work, and VTE terminal handling.
- These are behavioral patterns, not copies of UpdateManager source files. UpdateManager source headers identify GPL-2-or-later.
- Reference: /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/UpdateManager and /usr/share/update-manager/gtkbuilder on Ubuntu systems.

GNOME Baobab chart visualizations
- Rings is adapted from GNOME Baobab 49.1, the Disk Usage Analyzer installed by Ubuntu. Its annular-sector geometry, depth limits, minimum angle, continuation markers, palette, and interaction model informed gem/rings_view.py.
- Treemap and Rings share Baobab's position/depth palette through gem/chart_colors.py. Treemap uses the first-level x-position coloring from baobab-treemap.vala, with readable label colors and pagination rather than a status-colored geometry. The adjacent tree/chart layout and synchronized rerooting follow baobab-window.vala's interaction model.
- Copyright (C) 2008 Igalia; 2013 Stefano Facchini. The adapted chart implementations are distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later. See licenses/GPL-2.0.txt and licenses/GPL-3.0.txt.
- Source: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/baobab/-/blob/49.1/src/baobab-ringschart.vala, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/baobab/-/blob/49.1/src/baobab-treemap.vala, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/baobab/-/blob/49.1/src/baobab-chart.vala, and https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/baobab/-/blob/49.1/src/baobab-window.vala
- GEM uses investigation-subtree node counts, not bytes or analysis coverage, and adds explicit selection outlines, node-count captions, keyboard navigation, and accessible descriptions.

