Terminal palettes
- Tango, Linux console, and XTerm palette choices use their conventional named ANSI color arrangements.
- Solarized dark and light use the Solarized colors by Ethan Schoonover.
- Solarized source and license: https://github.com/altercation/solarized and licenses/Solarized-MIT.txt (MIT).
- The high-contrast palette is a GEM-specific arrangement. Color preferences are applied through VTE; no terminal emulator source files are copied.

GEM does not use xdg-open for untrusted artifacts. Show in Files uses Nautilus with --select after an explicit user action.
